  "body": "## What\n\n- `session.select@1` raises `notFound`, `noMatchingOption`, `ambiguousOption`, `optionDisabled`, and `notNativeSelect`. No `idempotent` marker: Playwright's `selectOption` fires `change` on every call.\n- New `session.legacySelect@1` with the same input shape, output `{}`, raises `notFound`.\n- Regenerated `Dsl.json`, `Dsl.py`, and `action_refs.py` with the new ref.\n\n## Why\n\n- The action side of the [BE-3483](https://linear.app/sola-ai/issue/BE-3483) decision record. The converter layer needs both refs.\n\n## Notes\n\n- `legacySelect` has its own input and output schemas, so the generated `SessionSelectV1Input` and `SessionSelectV1Output` files are identical to master's and two `SessionLegacySelectV1` files are added. Nothing generated is renamed or deleted.\n- `sessionLegacySelect` uses the click lookup policy, `REJECT_DISABLED_ONLY` with zero-area promotion, because V1 ran one lookup for Select and Click.\n- `sessionSelect` keeps `REJECT_HIDDEN_AND_DISABLED` without promotion.\n- The `$error` body carries `value`, `matchCount`, and the observed `options`, so a failed run shows what the page offered. `ActionError` is a loose object and `ErrorOutputs` admits only the `$error` port, so diagnostics nest inside it.\n- Additive, `session.select@1` keeps its input shape.\n\n## Examples\n\nThe converted Ferrara step and its fail-closed twin, target `select#test-report-action0` from workflow `d6e07303-729b-4936-bdb2-dce304fd8043`.\n\n```json\n{ \"kind\": \"action\", \"action\": \"session.legacySelect@1\",\n  \"in\": { \"session\": { \"kind\": \"var\", \"id\": \"v_session\" }, \"target\": { \"kind\": \"var\", \"id\": \"testReportAction0\" }, \"value\": { \"kind\": \"lit\", \"value\": \"Manage Documents\" } } }\n```\n\n```json\n{ \"kind\": \"action\", \"action\": \"session.select@1\",\n  \"in\": { \"session\": { \"kind\": \"var\", \"id\": \"v_session\" }, \"target\": { \"kind\": \"var\", \"id\": \"testReportAction0\" }, \"value\": { \"kind\": \"lit\", \"value\": \"Manage Docs\" } } }\n```\n\nOutcome of the second step against the fixture control:\n\n```json\n{ \"outcome\": \"$error\",\n  \"outputs\": {\n    \"$error\": {\n      \"type\": \"noMatchingOption\", \"message\": \"Select option did not match\",\n      \"value\": \"Manage Docs\",\n      \"matchCount\": 0,\n      \"options\": [\n        { \"text\": \"-- Choose --\", \"value\": \"0\", \"disabled\": false },\n        { \"text\": \"Create Check Call\", \"value\": \"9\", \"disabled\": false },\n        { \"text\": \"Create Note\", \"value\": \"4\", \"disabled\": false },\n        { \"text\": \"Finalize Load\", \"value\": \"13\", \"disabled\": false },\n        { \"text\": \"Request Rate Change\", \"value\": \"10\", \"disabled\": false },\n        { \"text\": \"Manage Documents\", \"value\": \"11\", \"disabled\": false },\n        { \"text\": \"View History\", \"value\": \"3\", \"disabled\": false } ] } } }\n```\n\nEvery outcome of `session.select@1` on that control:\n\n| `value` | Outcome | `matchCount` |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `Manage Documents` | `$ok {}` | |\n| `11` | `$ok {}` | |\n| `Manage Docs` | `$error noMatchingOption` | 0 |\n| `Manage Documents` while that option is disabled | `$error optionDisabled` | 1 |\n| `New Jersey` against two options with different values | `$error ambiguousOption` | 2 |\n| any value with the target on a `<div>` | `$error notNativeSelect`, `tagName: \"div\"` | |\n| any value with the target missing | `$error notFound` | |\n\n## Testing\n\nGrid run of the two-backend action matrix on the compose Selenium Grid, both actions, including hidden-select `notFound`. The skips are the Playwright half of the matrix. Log noise trimmed.\n\n```text\n$ vitest run --project integration\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  26 passed | 32 skipped (58)\n   Start at  09:53:19\n   Duration  27.02s (transform 631ms, setup 0ms, import 1.06s, tests 25.88s, environment 0ms)\n```\n",
